{
  "comment": "The recorded-invocation gate. Each scenario is one offline invocation: argv, environment, and recorded responses. The stage 1 scenarios were generated by the TypeScript implementation this package replaced and remain the cross-language parity gate (docs/design/v1-python.md \u00a75); the stage 2 host, vuln, and scopes scenarios and the stage 3 NG-SIEM search scenarios are regression pins generated from this implementation. Four stage 1 documents changed at stage 2 (help-top, unknown-command, home-view, home-view-no-credential) because the command surface grew to the one docs/design/v1.md \u00a71.4 specifies, and eight changed at stage 3 (those four plus scopes, auth-status, auth-status-member-cid, auth-status-retargeted) because captain exception N1 added the NG-SIEM search surface and the NGSIEM:write scope it requires (docs/design/v1.md \u00a74.3). help-vuln-list changed when vuln list gained --fields (docs/design/v1.md \u00a710). help-top, unknown-command, home-view, and scopes changed when cve show shipped: the command list, the home suggestion, and the license-gated Falcon Intelligence scope (docs/design/v1.md \u00a72.2). Stage 4 slice B added the identity scenarios and changed help-top, unknown-command, scopes, and the three auth-status documents that print a scope line, because captain exception N2 added the `identity` noun and the Identity Protection GraphQL:write scope it requires (docs/design/v1.md \u00a74.4). host-list-filtered and identity-list changed to shell-safe continuation quoting, preserving wildcard arguments literally (docs/design/v1.md \u00a77.2). identity-list's cursor changed to bind an unambiguous JSON filter tuple (docs/design/v1.md \u00a74.4), and scopes changed to describe only the effect of omitting NGSIEM:write, without claiming the remaining GraphQL write permission is read-only (docs/design/v1.md \u00a75.7). help-search-start and help-search-stop changed to state their NGSIEM:write requirement without claiming it is the tool's only write scope (docs/design/v1.md \u00a74.3). Identity slice A adds identity-activity, identity detection, and --product scenarios (docs/design/v1.md sections 4.3 and 10.2). Its help, command-discovery, home, auth, and scopes changes are combined with slice B rather than replacing that surface. help-identity-activity states only its command-specific NGSIEM:write requirement, without claiming it is the tool's only write scope (section 4.3). Identity detection rows include account_id and device_id and omit the unrequested source_ip field. Shared suggestions preserve literal FQL and backticks, explicit region and origin opt-in, and tenant selection without printing a standalone CID (section 7.2).",
